From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: umd: provide a gettid() fallback for glibc older than 2.30

The [tid:] field in the NPU_LOG output calls gettid() directly, both from
the _LOG macro in umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp and from roughly
500 places in the generated umd/level_zero_driver/api/trace/ headers.

glibc only provides the gettid() wrapper from 2.30 onwards; the syscall
itself has always been available. Building against an older glibc fails on
essentially every translation unit whenever ENABLE_NPU_LOGGING is set,
which is the default:

    error: 'gettid' was not declared in this scope; did you mean 'getuid'?

This affects anyone targeting an older baseline than the build host, which
is common when packaging binaries intended to run on a range of
distributions.

Supply the missing wrapper in log.hpp, guarded on the glibc version. That
covers every call site without touching the generated headers, since they
all reach log.hpp through trace_ze_api.hpp, and so it also survives those
headers being regenerated. On glibc 2.30 and newer the fallback is not
compiled at all, leaving behaviour unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>

---
 umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)
diff --git a/umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp b/umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp
index c8af5b8..60359c1 100644
--- a/umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp
+++ b/umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp
@@ -12,8 +12,26 @@
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <string_view>
+#include <sys/syscall.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 
+/*
+ * glibc only provides the gettid() wrapper from 2.30 onwards; the syscall
+ * itself has always been there. Supply the wrapper on older C libraries so
+ * the driver still builds against an older sysroot (conda-forge, for
+ * instance, packages against a glibc 2.17 sysroot to keep the binaries
+ * usable on older distributions).
+ *
+ * Defining it here covers every NPU_LOG call site: the _LOG macro below,
+ * and the generated umd/level_zero_driver/api/trace/ headers, which all
+ * reach this header through trace_ze_api.hpp.
+ */
+#if defined(__GLIBC__) && (__GLIBC__ < 2 || (__GLIBC__ == 2 && __GLIBC_MINOR__ < 30))
+static inline pid_t gettid() {
+    return static_cast<pid_t>(syscall(SYS_gettid));
+}
+#endif
+
 enum LogLevel { QUIET = 0, ERROR, WARNING, INFO };
 
 #define BIT(nr) ((1UL) << (nr))
